"A canon is a technique that employs a melody with one or more imitations of the melody. The first melody is the leader, and the imitating melody, in a different voice, is the follower. In the Taiwan dictionary, one voice comes first, and the other voices join with the same melody in turn, chasing one another to the last bar. A round is a limited type of canon: many voices sing exactly the same melody, each beginning at a different time. A voice here means a single melodic line.": "f7acf4f2ba65",
"A cantata has singers and instruments.": "9e94aa817b41",
"A fugue is built on a subject.": "82f44313cddd",
"A round has no fixed ending.": "bdf2b9b4ae4e",
"Bach was an organ player.": "d5317ff908fb",
"Bach’s music encompasses every genre of his time aside from opera. He wrote extensively for the organ and other keyboard instruments, and he also wrote orchestral and chamber music. He is known for his mastery of counterpoint. Many of his works use techniques like canon and fugue, which he did not invent but contributed to so fundamentally as to influence many followers.": "17f5a37c13c1",
"Counterpoint is the relationship of two or more simultaneous musical lines. The lines depend on each other harmonically, yet they are independent in rhythm and melodic contour. A fugue is a technique in two or more voices built on a subject, which then sounds successively in each voice. The word comes from the Latin fuga, “flight”, and from the verbs for “to flee” and “to chase”. A fugue is closer to a style of composition than to a fixed form, so in this lesson we only play with canons.": "a27d4255f8ba",
"Counterpoint joins independent melodies.": "e4114a9eafc4",
"Each voice sings its own line.": "fc052940bd6d",
"In 1703 Bach became the organist at the New Church. He returned to Weimar as court organist in 1708, and he became a director of music in 1717. In 1723 he was appointed Thomaskantor, the director of church music in Leipzig, and he held that position for 27 years, until his death. He directed the St. Thomas School and provided four churches with music. A cantata was required for the church services on each Sunday, and his body of work includes more than 200 cantatas.": "a460450ed44d",
